From 6c88d68f7b59295326515467f20add595a14c3ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:35:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build the public site and make the quote form real

Milestone 2. Home, Our Work, Products, product detail, Process, About and
FAQ, carrying the copy from the approved design and reading products and
portfolio items from the database rather than hard-coded arrays.

The quote form is the part that actually does something: it validates
server-side, stores the enquiry under a human-readable reference, emails a
confirmation to the sender and the enquiry itself to the studio, attaches
to the signed-in account when there is one, and shows up in the customer's
Quotes page where they can withdraw it while it is still open.

Notable decisions:

- Photography isn't in yet, so image slots render as labelled placeholders
  carrying the caption from the design. Swapping one for a real photograph
  is a one-line change at the call site.
- Terms, privacy and cookies exist as pages but say plainly that the
  wording must come from the studio. Boilerplate there could assert things
  about the business that aren't true.
- Visitor-supplied text is escaped before it goes into an email body; a
  crafted enquiry could otherwise inject markup into the studio's inbox.
- Rate limits are now read from the environment, defaults unchanged. The
  test suite signs in far more often than a person would, so it raises them
  for its own server rather than weakening the app.

Two bugs the tests caught and fixed: an untouched optional quantity field
submitted "" and failed validation, and the mobile menu closed via an
effect that triggered cascading renders.

Covered by 29 Playwright tests and 4 unit tests for the limiter.

